    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Subtype</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Logic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Defs</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">DefEqTransformations</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a_iso_graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Bijective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Injective</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">beta_reduce</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- this unfold graph is VERY IMPORTANT</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- lean cannot see that graph f is a subtype unless you do this unfold,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- which changes nothing in the infoview so you think it is not actually</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- doing anything</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- rewrite rules for (a, b).1 = a are hidden away in Lean.Omega for some</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- reason</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rewrite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subtype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk_eq_mk</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Prod</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ext_iff</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Omega</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Prod</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst_mk</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Omega</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Prod</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst_mk</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Omega</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Prod</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd_mk</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Omega</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Prod</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd_mk</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">left</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Surjective</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">beta_reduce</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩⟩</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- for various reasons it's easier if we use the a from the ∃ clause</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- much like earlier this unfold is very important</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ext1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">push_cast</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592796339,
        "sender_full_name": "incertia",
        "timestamp": 1777915357
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i'm vaguely aware that <code>abbrev</code> also works, are they preferred for type-level functions?</p>",
        "id": 592796522,
        "sender_full_name": "incertia",
        "timestamp": 1777915410
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i think the main question from me is whether or not the lean infoview should show what the type looks like to whatever tactic you are running next (much like your hypotheses and goals) rather than the fully unfolded type</p>",
        "id": 592796727,
        "sender_full_name": "incertia",
        "timestamp": 1777915474
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i.e. when hovering over the subtype in h in L11, the infoview says its value is constructed with <a href=\"http://Subtype.mk\">Subtype.mk</a> and its type is in <code>{p // ...}</code> notation, none of which suggest that the next tactics would see it as <code>graph f</code> rather than <code>Subtype</code></p>",
        "id": 592798759,
        "sender_full_name": "incertia",
        "timestamp": 1777915995
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure if this will answer your question but generally when you make a <code>def</code>, you are responsible for making the API to work with it (as opposed to an <code>abbrev</code> which things like rewrite can \"see through\"). In this case, you could do something like this.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Subtype</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Logic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Defs</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">DefEqTransformations</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ext_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subtype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ext_iff</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a_iso_graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Bijective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Injective</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">beta_reduce</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rewrite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ext_iff</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">left</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Surjective</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">beta_reduce</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rewrite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ext_iff</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">push_cast</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592804430,
        "sender_full_name": "Brian Nugent",
        "timestamp": 1777917327
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also the <code>unfold</code> and <code>beta_reduce</code> lines are unnecessary</p>",
        "id": 592805066,
        "sender_full_name": "Brian Nugent",
        "timestamp": 1777917492
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>we had this problem with <code>NNReal</code> recently, see <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/backward.2EisDefEq.2ErespectTransparency/near/583580618\">#general &gt; backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency @ 💬</a></p>",
        "id": 592806494,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777917797
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1003282\">Brian Nugent</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/lean.20infoview.20hover.20type.20unfolding/near/592804430\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>when you make a <code>def</code>, you are responsible for making the API to work with it (as opposed to an <code>abbrev</code> which things like rewrite can \"see through\").</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I can agree with this. It is probably worth discussing if the lean infoview fully unfolding a type is the <em>correct</em> behavior though, especially when that type is not unfolded for the upcoming tactic.</p>",
        "id": 592822833,
        "sender_full_name": "incertia",
        "timestamp": 1777922409
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i.e. when you hover over <code>h</code> in <code>intro a b h</code> on L14 in the 2nd example<br>\n<img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"703x234\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/QtbZ72_pXU6DXaQWIdehYvek/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/QtbZ72_pXU6DXaQWIdehYvek/image.png/840x560.webp\"></p>",
        "id": 592823150,
        "sender_full_name": "incertia",
        "timestamp": 1777922498
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>perhaps it should say <code>: graph f</code> instead of <code>: {p // ∃a, (a, f a) = p}</code></p>",
        "id": 592823792,
        "sender_full_name": "incertia",
        "timestamp": 1777922682
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree that is confusing. FWIW, if you hover over the type of <code>h</code> you will get <code>@Eq (graph f) ⟨(a, f a), ⋯⟩ ⟨(b, f b), ⋯⟩</code></p>",
        "id": 592829610,
        "sender_full_name": "Brian Nugent",
        "timestamp": 1777924549
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For your use case, you probably want to either define <code>graph</code> as a set (i.e. of type <code>Set α × β</code>) or make it an abbrev. I'd probably go with the former.</p>",
        "id": 592830032,
        "sender_full_name": "Brian Nugent",
        "timestamp": 1777924689
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I see, I need to hover over the = and not the specific term</p>",
        "id": 592834667,
        "sender_full_name": "incertia",
        "timestamp": 1777926090
    }
]